          <div style="margin-top:11.8pt; text-align:justify; width:456pt; line-height:11.5pt;">
            <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">An increase of $0.25 in the assumed public offering price of $1.15 per share, which is the last reported trading price of our common stock on the Nasdaq Capital Market on September&#160;7, 2023, would increase our as adjusted net tangible book value per share after this offering by $0.13 and result in dilution to new investors purchasing shares in this offering of $0.20 per share, while a decrease of $0.25 would decrease our as adjusted net tangible book value per share after this offering by $0.34 per share and result in dilution to new investors purchasing shares in this offering of $0.17 per share, all assuming that the number of shares offered by us, as set forth on the cover page of this prospectus, remains the same and after deducting estimated underwriting discounts and commissions and estimated expenses payable by us.</font>
          </div>


          <div style="margin-top:12pt; text-align:justify; width:456pt; line-height:11.5pt;">
            <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">An increase (decrease) of one million shares in the number of shares offered by us in this offering would both result in our as adjusted net tangible book value per share being $1.01 with immediate dilution to investors participating in this offering of $0.14 per share. The foregoing calculations assume that the public offering price remains the same, and are after deducting estimated underwriting discounts and commissions and estimated expenses payable by us. </font>
          </div>


          <div style="margin-top:12pt; text-align:justify; width:456pt; line-height:11.5pt;">
            <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">If the underwriter&#8217;s over-allotment option is exercised in full, our as adjusted net tangible book value per share after this offering would be approximately $12.1 million and there would be no additional dilutive or antidilutive effect per share to new investors purchasing common stock in this offering. These calculations assume a public offering price of $1.15 per share, the last reported sale price of our common stock on the Nasdaq Capital Market on September&#160;7, 2023, and are after deducting the estimated underwriting discounts and commissions and estimated offering expenses payable by us. </font>
          </div>

      </div>
